.TH YLR-AUTO 1 "November 2026" "YLR-Auto 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ylr-auto \- companion for MakeMKV that files finished rips into Jellyfin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ylr-auto
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.br
.B ylr-auto
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ylr-auto
shows what MakeMKV and each optical drive are doing, then files finished rips
into Jellyfin libraries using names and posters from TMDb. Films that match
exactly one TMDb entry by name and runtime can be filed automatically, and
anything uncertain waits for you. MakeMKV is a separate program and is not
included.
.PP
Closing the window keeps the program monitoring from the tray. Use the tray
menu to quit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start in the tray with no window. Login startup uses this.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMDB_API_KEY
TMDb API key or read access token. Overrides the saved key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/littlerippa\-autosort/config.json
Settings, including the TMDb key. Readable by the owner only.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/littlerippa\-autosort/autosort.log
Record of rips and file moves.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/littlerippa\-autosort/posters
Cached TMDb posters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR makemkvcon (1)
.PP
https://github.com/cpntodd/YLR\-Auto
